      <h2>About House of Wonders</h2>
      <div>Beit-al-Ajaib (House of Wonders) is Stone Town's most iconic landmark — a grand ceremonial palace built in 1883 for Sultan Barghash bin Said. It was the first building in Zanzibar to have electricity and an elevator, hence its name. The massive coral stone structure with its distinctive verandas and clock tower dominates the waterfront. Currently undergoing UNESCO-supported restoration; the exterior courtyard and ground floor are accessible, offering glimpses of its former grandeur and Swahili-Omani architecture.</div>
